# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit real values.

# Live rating badge in the header — Places API (New), place details.
# Both must be present or the badge renders nothing. The key is only ever read on the
# server; it is never sent to the browser. The key must be restricted to the Places API
# and, once hosting is settled, to the server's address.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=
# The café's Place ID. Not a secret: it resolves to "Zukis Caffetteria, 3B Queen St,
# Exeter EX4 3SB" and is the same for everyone.
GOOGLE_PLACE_ID=ChIJRxz9-QClbUgRigJpc1wN0pc

# Table bookings. "manual": a person at the café confirms each request (the interim
# setting while the capacity rules are provisional). "instant": the table is held on
# submission — the requirement, switched on once the café has confirmed the rules.
BOOKING_CONFIRMATION=manual

# Microsoft Clarity analytics. Public configuration, not a secret, but not hard-coded: with
# it empty nothing loads and nothing breaks. Loaded only after "Accept all"; the booking
# form is masked. In GitHub Actions it is the repository variable CLARITY_PROJECT_ID.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=

# Deployment to Cloudflare (docs/access.md). Only needed to deploy from a workstation;
# the GitHub Actions workflow reads the same two values from repository secrets.
# The token is scoped to the Vegasoft account only, with Workers Scripts, D1, R2 and
# Workers KV edit permissions and no zone permissions. Revoke and re-issue rather than
# share it.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
